=========================================================================
(b) NO INLINE NEGATED SUM REMAINS  -- FAIL
=========================================================================
The brief's grep, run on the real tree:
  grep -n "= -[a-zA-Z]*[.(]\|-sumSigned(\|SumAmount()" \
       internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go
returns, among comment lines, a live code line the manifest never mentions:

  1522:		monthlyTotals[m] = -monthlyOutflowSets[m].SumAmount()

(in `buildSpendingTrendChartData`, served by GET
/dashboard/charts/data/spending-trend). An exhaustive negation sweep
  grep -nE '(=|\(|,|return|\+=|-=)[[:space:]]*-[a-zA-Z_]|[-][=][[:space:]]' \
       internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go | grep -v '^[0-9]*:[[:space:]]*//'
yields exactly five non-comment negations:
   403: total -= t.Amount                       (accumulator, safe)
  1340: total += -t.Amount                      (accumulator, safe)
  1401: unmatchedTotal += -t.Amount             (accumulator, safe)
  1522: monthlyTotals[m] = -...SumAmount()      **INLINE NEGATED SUM, NOT ROUTED**
  1598: merchantTotals[t.Label()] -= t.Amount   (accumulator, safe)

So the brief's own statement that "the two `+= -t.Amount` accumulators
(1340, 1401) are the only negations" is factually false in two ways: there
are FOUR accumulators (403 and 1598 were not enumerated by the manifest,
though both are safe by the same argument), and there is a fifth, unfixed
inline negated sum at 1522.

PROOF THAT 1522 PRODUCES AN OBSERVABLE -0, using CB9's OWN fixture
(`cb9CancellingRows`, in-package probe hitting the real chi route):
  GET /dashboard/charts/data/spending-trend?start=2025-01-01&end=2025-02-28
  -> 200, body:
     {"data":[{"customdata":[[-0,520]], ... "hovertemplate":
      "...Spent: $%{customdata[0]:,.0f}<br>Prior: $%{customdata[1]:,.0f}..."}]}
  The served JSON literally contains the token `-0`. Its source is the
  February all-outflow bucket, which my type/sum probe shows nets exactly
  IEEE -0:
     PROBE ALLOUT month=2025-02 rawNeg=-0 signbit=true signedNet=0 n=4
  This is the SAME layer the CB9 tests themselves treat as a defect:
  `TestHandleKPIMonthDetail_CB9_...` fails a response whose JSON "carries
  a -0 token", justified as "a JSON consumer or a raw formatter would
  surface the sign". CB9 asserts that for the KPI month-detail endpoint
  and leaves the identical token in the spending-trend chart endpoint.

  Rendered-surface note (disclosed, not decisive): I decompiled the
  d3-format copy inside data/cache/plotly.min.js and found the guard
  `m&&0==+t&&"+"!==n&&(m=!1)` (d3-format's "clear valueNegative when the
  formatted value is zero and sign spec is not '+'"), so the hovertemplate
  `$%{customdata[0]:,.0f}` would render "$0", not "$-0". The defect is
  therefore at the JSON/API layer, not the pixel layer -- but that is
  exactly the layer CB9's own month-detail test polices.

  This site is NOT excluded by the spec. `.swarm/CB7-RUN-SPEC.md` "Not in
  scope" names only the **`prev > 0` guard at handlers.go:1533** in this
  same function (percent-change product semantics, reclassified
  2026-09-03) -- a different line addressing a different question. The -0
  at 1522 falls squarely under the CB9 contract sentence "every
  negated-sum spend site in internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go
  routes through metrics.SignedNet".

ACCUMULATOR ARGUMENT -- I AGREE, AND IT IS PROVEN.
`go run` on a throwaway module (scratchpad/zeroprobe):
  after += -0.0      : v=0 signbit=false %.2f=0.00
  after += -100,+100 : v=0 signbit=false %.2f=0.00
  accum with true -0 : v=0 signbit=false      (+0 + (-0) = +0, IEEE 754)
  -= form            : v=0 signbit=false      (covers 403 and 1598)
  inline -sum        : v=-0 signbit=true %.2f=-0.00   <-- the 1522 shape
An accumulator declared `var x float64` starts at +0; (+0)+(-0)=+0 and
x+(-x)=+0 in round-to-nearest, so no accumulator can land on -0. The
inline `-(sum)` form provably can, and does.

