  M4  :943  expAmt = -exp.SumAmount()          (handleKPIExport)
        -> FAIL: TestHandleKPIExport_CB9_CancellingMonthWritesPositiveZero
  M5  :1109 hcAmt = -hc.SumAmount()            -> SURVIVES (ok)
  M6  :1119 livingMonth = -lo.SumAmount()      -> SURVIVES (ok)
  M7  :1160 spend = -bucket.SumAmount()        -> SURVIVES (ok)
  M8  render.go formatPercent belt deleted
        -> FAIL: render_helpers_test.go:165: formatPercent(-0) = "-0.0",
           want "0.0"  (TestFormatPercent)  [restored, then ok]

The unobservability argument for M5/M6 does NOT hold. `hcAmt` and
`livingMonth` are appended straight into `healthcareValues` /
`livingValues`, which become the Plotly traces' `y` arrays -- no
subtraction absorbs the sign. Direct call to
`buildBudgetVsActualChartData(filtered, 2025-01-01, 2025-02-28, 400, 350,
coverageStart, true, nil)` on the CB9 fixture:
  with the fix   : "name":"Living",...,"y":[220,0]
                   "name":"Healthcare",...,"y":[300,0]
  with M5+M6     : "name":"Living",...,"y":[220,-0]
                   "name":"Healthcare",...,"y":[300,-0]
So those two fixes ARE consumer-observable at the served-JSON layer and
are simply untested. The lead's own written acceptance line in
`.swarm/CB7-RUN-SPEC.md` ("every SignedNet site load-bearing by mutation
or provably consumer-unobservable") is therefore unmet at :1109 and :1119.
Only M7 (`spend`) qualifies as unobservable: its sole use is
`running += monthTarget - spend`, and `x - (-0) == x - 0` for every x, so
the sign never reaches `cumulativeValues`. I accept M7's survival on the
CB7 precedent; I do not accept M5/M6's on the stated argument, because the
stated argument ("subtraction absorbs -0") is false for those two.
Note the code at :1109/:1119 is CORRECT -- this is a coverage/justification
gap, not a wrong figure.

