(d) NEW TESTS ASSERT WHAT THEY CLAIM  -- PASS
=========================================================================
Read /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/internal/handlers/dashboard/cb9_negzero_http_test.go
in full. Assertions are on RENDERED strings (CSV cells parsed with
encoding/csv, compared to the literal "0.00" and prefix-checked for "-0"),
on the raw JSON body (regexp `-0(\.0+)?[,}\]\s]`), and on the decoded
float's sign bit (`math.Signbit`). No float-only assertions substituted
for a displayed figure.

The fixture is NOT vacuous. In-package probe dumping `TransactionType`
after the real dataloader/classifier ran on `cb9CancellingRows()`:
  date=2025-02-15 desc="Health Insurance Premium"        amt=-300.00 cat=Health Insurance type=Outflow
  date=2025-02-20 desc="Health Insurance Premium Credit" amt= 300.00 cat=Health Insurance type=Outflow
  date=2025-02-10 desc="Groceries"                       amt=-100.00 cat=Food             type=Outflow
  date=2025-02-12 desc="Store Credit"                    amt= 100.00 cat=Food             type=Outflow
Both credit rows are Outflow-typed (the "Premium Credit" / "Store Credit"
wording avoids the classifier's income keywords), so February really nets
exactly zero at every slicing, and it nets IEEE -0 before the fix:
  PROBE ALLOUT month=2025-02 rawNeg=-0 signbit=true signedNet=0 n=4
  PROBE HC     month=2025-02 rawNeg=-0 signbit=true      n=2
  PROBE LIVING month=2025-02 rawNeg=-0 signbit=true      n=2
January (rawNeg=520 / 300 / 220, signbit=false) keeps the range
net-spend, so the fixture is not degenerate. Mutations M1-M4 above prove
the tests are load-bearing rather than merely present.

`render_helpers_test.go` adds `{math.Copysign(0, -1), "0.0"}` to
TestFormatPercent's table -- a real -0, killed by M8.

