(e) MCP DOC COMMENT MATCHES THE IMPLEMENTED RULE  -- PASS
=========================================================================
`internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/trends.go:80-89` now documents:
  (window - history) / |history| * 100 when history is non-zero; when
  history is exactly zero it is +100 / -100 / 0 by the sign of the change
  (ruling CB8-2026-09-03a).
`internal/services/insights/trends.go:355-366` implements exactly:
  change := dailyAvg - historicalDaily
  case historicalDaily != 0: change / math.Abs(historicalDaily) * 100
  case change > 0: 100 ; case change < 0: -100 ; default: 0
And `trends.go:142-146` `velocityRowFrom` sets
`BurnRateChange: round2(v.BurnRateChange)` straight from
`*models.SpendingVelocity`, so the documented type IS the one produced by
that code path. Denominator (|history|) and zero-base rule both match.

